{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/940212-unchosen-unbidden-unloved-doubting-souls","id":940212,"title":"Unchosen, Unbidden, Unloved [Doubting Souls]","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-07-30T13:21:36-07:00","id":940212,"title":"Unchosen, Unbidden, Unloved [Doubting Souls]","content":"warning- contains spoilers from Tales of the Dark Eras, so if you didn't read the anthology and plan to do so, stop reading right here. The God Machine thanks you for your corporation.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> So, in the Doubting Souls chapter in the book, we are presented with an interesting plot hook- three dead bodies of children which are lying beneath the local Church, each named as Unchosen, Unbidden or Unloved, with the sidebar describing that no human dead or alive knows that they are buried there and why. Now, when I first read it I was sure it would be just an interesting piece of the setting without any consequences, and that we are never going to hear about them again. However, I was wrong- and in Suffering of the Unchosen from the anthology we discover that the last sentence, as you may have wondered, was more meaningful than it seems- for the one who knows about the three and their goal is not a human: it's a demon, and one we are all familiar with. Mister White.<br /> <br /> From what we know, Mister White has a strong motif of punishment- although it may be the influence of his last Cover, but it still somehow works within the story. We also know that for some reason, Mister White has the ability to command the three, and that they seem to be able to hold a lot of power in them- and his plan for that power is important enough that he had to use the chaos of the Witch Trails and turn the Knights against the Scarlet Watch (I'm pretty sure it was them, both because of Mary being a vampire and another small thing I'll discuses later) so he could use them undisturbed. It does not, however, tells us anything about who/ what the three are or what is going to happen (Mister White is going to survive this, 'cause you know- he is present in the modern time). Also, from the ending, it is pretty clear how the things are supposed to happen from that point in time- Mister White rise the three and use the chaos and disunity he fed with his scheme to turn the hunters upon each other and bring a potential disaster to the place. However, while such path of &quot;ultimate disaster rise during infighting&quot; is interesting to explore, there is another path- one in which the hunters actually rise above their differences and stop the demon in time, and I think there is a justification for it within the given story. The reason? Mister Whiter has made a mistake.<br /> <br /> It's not a big mistake- actually, it is one that is easy to overlook, allowing you to play both scenarios. You need to be smart in order to catch that mistake, with attention to details and be able to let go of the natural distrust between the many hunter groups of the Era- for even if you understand it, it doesn't necessary mean you are able to convince the others, especially the Knights (unless you are part of them) that you are right and they are wrong. The mistake is, that while fighting with one of the Scarlet Watch hunters, Mister White said that he wandered how many innocents were killed during their &quot;watch&quot;- with an emphasis around that word. Considering that he acted as if he knew nothing about the Vigil and the occult societies of the time and place, the fact he chose that word may be enough to rise suspicion- and perhaps enough to create some unwanted attention- in the form of the player characters. Of course, chaotic mild-apocalyptic scene is also appropriate and may be fun to play.<br /> <br /> And of course, we also need to decide what exactly are the Unchosen, Unbidden and the Unloved. The fact they could be controlled by Mister White hints for a demonic/God Machine origin, but the exact nature itself is open for interpretation.<br /> <br /> So- what do you think? Will Mister White succeed in his plot? What is his plan exactly? And what those three apparently dead children actually can do which is enough to invest all of that effort in increasing the already boiling paranoia of the hunters in the setting?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-30T14:38:24-07:00","id":940262,"title":"","content":"Mr. White honestly strikes me as one of the Infernal demons, more-he can be sympathetic, but at his core, White's more a symbol than a person. He's the self-destructive nature of vengeance-corrupting-justice made flesh. He has no reason, he simply is-if he is at the moment. In the story, we can see he doesn't always remember he's not his host, and the modern Mr. White hasn't seemed able to break the facade as much as he'd like.<br /> <br /> My guess is the reason he started branding the Three U zombies is that something about the Salem trials called to his nature, and now he is driven to animate the bodies of innocents killed by the misguided (Unchosen, Unbidden, and Unloved by humanity enough to spare them) to complete the cycle that was begun by the witch trials and bring their regretful destroyers down with them. That he must occasionally see to it that the cycle continues in his projected way does not strike him as a paradox-it is simply the way he is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}